#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Start a read-only model worker for OSS research inside the sandbox runtime.

The model CLI is a backend (BACKENDS: claude, codex, agy; --backend, default
claude). Everything the runner knows about one CLI (its executable, argv,
configuration home, credential variable, model endpoint, result shape) sits
behind that Backend; the module constants below are the Claude backend's
values, unchanged. Only the Claude backend has a measured launch: a request
for another backend is Blocked at the gate like any other unmeasured launch,
with the credential unread, and the Claude path is byte for byte what it was.

The real launch is closed except for the launches listed in MEASURED_LAUNCHES.
The pinned srt install and the shape of a profile-bound credential file are
checked first. Then only a request that equals a measured launch in every field
reads the credential and starts: on Linux, the Debian 13 guest, read-only,
dontAsk, no relay, claude-profile2, claude-opus-5-5 at medium, inside the unit
wrapper, with the measured node and Claude files. macOS has no measured launch,
so main stays closed there. Everything else stays behind the gate: auto, a
relay, the corpus-extract and deep-research profiles (reviewed skill sources
staged under a hash pin, writes to them denied), another profile, model or
effort. SYSTEM_READ_MEASURED["linux"] is False: the Linux read set counts as
measured for that one launch only, not in general. The code that hands the
credential to the child and checks it was not exposed runs in tests with fake
sentinels and in that measured launch. See docs/oss-research-worker.md.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import base64
